\title{A FIMS module}
\description{
Every \verb{create_*()} function returns a \code{fims_module} --- a fleet,
a population, a selectivity curve --- that lives on the C++ side.
The return from \verb{create_*()} points to the C++ module directly (not a copy).

That reference behaviour is worth knowing, because it differs from most R
objects. If you write \code{b <- a}, you have not made a second module. Both
names refer to the same one, and a value set through \code{b} is visible through
\code{a}. Modules are changed by passing them to a setter, never by assigning to
their parts, and you should not edit the fields of a \code{fims_module}
yourself.
